  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 1; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels \\(6\\) shrimp per minute for \\(10\\) minutes:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nSince she has \\(100\\) shrimp available, she can peel and sauté all \\(60\\) shrimp she processes.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60 \\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nShe then discards \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60 - 5 = 55 \\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSo, Emily peels \\(\\boxed{60\\text{ shrimp}}\\), with \\(\\boxed{55\\text{ shrimp}}\\) remaining after discarding the damaged ones.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily’s sautéing rate is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp per minute}.\n\\]\n\nIn \\(10\\) minutes, she can sauté\n\n\\[\n2.5 \\times 10=25\\text{ shrimp}.\n\\]\n\nShe can peel \\(60\\) shrimp in that time, and after discarding \\(5\\), \\(55\\) usable shrimp remain—more than enough for sautéing. Therefore, the sautéing capacity is the limiting factor:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp in ten minutes. After discarding \\(5\\), \\(55\\) usable shrimp remain.\n\nShe can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in ten minutes, so sautéing is the limiting step.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily works sequentially, peeling and sautéing times add together.\n\n- Peeling rate: \\(6\\) shrimp/minute, so peeling \\(x\\) shrimp takes \\(\\frac{x}{6}\\) minutes.\n- Sautéing rate: \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes, or \\(3\\) shrimp/minute, so sautéing \\(y\\) shrimp takes \\(\\frac{y}{3}\\) minutes.\n- To sauté \\(y\\) usable shrimp, she must peel \\(y+5\\) shrimp because \\(5\\) are discarded.\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\frac{y+5}{6}+\\frac{y}{3}\\le 10.\n\\]\n\nMultiplying by \\(6\\):\n\n\\[\ny+5+2y\\le 60\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3y\\le 55\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny\\le 18\\frac{1}{3}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the greatest whole number of shrimp she can peel and sauté is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18\\text{ shrimp}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To cook \\(90\\) usable shrimp, Emily must peel \\(95\\) shrimp because \\(5\\) are discarded.\n\nPeeling time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{95}{6}=15\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSautéing time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{3}=30\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nBecause she works sequentially, add the times:\n\n\\[\n15\\frac{5}{6}+30=45\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThat is \\(45\\) minutes and \\(50\\) seconds.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
